{"Priority-based provider selection is capability-agnostic - a high-priority provider can be selected even if it lacks required operations, causing runtime failures from partial implementations": 0.47997045516967773, "Consider adding capability validation at initialization time or implementing feature-based provider resolution to prevent runtime failures": 0.14795130491256714, "Initializing CryptoIntegration as a side effect of create() introduces global/static crypto setup that may not be expected by library consumers, creating classloader coupling or initialization-order issues in embedded runtimes": 0.46993669867515564, "The side effect of CryptoIntegration initialization should be documented in the method's Javadoc, or an explicit initialization method separate from client creation should be provided": 0.19822940230369568, "Minimal provider implements a broad interface with 15+ methods throwing UnsupportedOperationException, violating the Liskov Substitution Principle": 0.29738950729370117, "Consider splitting the SPI into smaller capability-specific interfaces to address the partial implementation problem": 0.011396093294024467, "Consider adding runtime guards/tests to ensure only supported methods are reachable in the minimal provider": 0.0030952547676861286, "Consider implementing capability discovery in the provider selection logic": 0.012478400953114033, "Provider precedence is controlled by numeric ordering constants across different modules without any mechanism to enforce or validate the contract": 0.12349164485931396, "Silent provider ignoring (debug-log only) hides potential misconfiguration in production deployments": 0.1790769100189209, "CryptoProvider interface semantics shifted from single complete provider to possibly partial prioritized provider but the interface and documentation don't communicate this change": 0.26223814487457275}